---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
const jsonLd = {"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Person","name":"Muhammad Babar","jobTitle":"Data & BI Consultant","url":"https://mbabar90.github.io/","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Lahore","addressCountry":"PK"},"sameAs":["https://www.linkedin.com/in/mubabar90","https://www.credly.com/users/muhammad-babar90","https://apexpaths.co"]};
---
<Base title="Muhammad Babar · Data & BI Consultant" description="Data and BI consultant in Lahore with 10+ years in actuarial and people analytics. Power BI, Power Query, Qlik, Alteryx and Python. Open to freelance, contract, part-time and full-time work." active="home" jsonLd={jsonLd}>
<section class="hero"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="hero-top">
    <div>
      <span class="lab eyebrow">Lahore, Pakistan · 10+ years in data</span>
      <h1><span>Muhammad</span><span>Babar</span></h1>
      <div class="lines">
        <span><b>Data &amp; BI consultant.</b></span>
        <span><i>Trained as an actuary.</i></span>
        <span><i>Builds apps after hours.</i></span>
      </div>
      <div class="cta">
        <a class="btn solid" href="#about">Get to know me</a>
        <a class="btn" href="#contact">Get in touch</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="sel">
      <span class="lab">Selected work</span>
      <a class="srow" href="/work/#employee-360"><b>1M+</b><div><strong>One history for every employee</strong><small>Engro · records matched across systems with no shared ID</small></div></a>
      <a class="srow" href="/work/#hr-reporting"><b>~70%</b><div><strong>Group HR reporting, automated</strong><small>Engro · less manual effort, more frequent reports</small></div></a>
      <a class="srow" href="/work/#alteryx"><b>~50%</b><div><strong>From macros to Alteryx</strong><small>SHMA · less time on routine actuarial reporting</small></div></a>
      <a class="srow" href="/work/#adnic"><b class="w">On schedule</b><div><strong>Appointed actuary work for ADNIC</strong><small>SHMA · regulatory deliverables for a major UAE insurer</small></div></a>
      <a class="more" href="/work/">All case studies →</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section class="band watch" id="apps"><div class="wrap">
  <span class="lab eyebrow">After hours · ApexPaths</span>
  <h2>Three apps. One in open beta.</h2>
  <p class="lead">Built under ApexPaths with Bismah Khalid. Each one answers a problem met at work or at home.</p>
  <div class="apps">
    <div class="fs">
      <div class="stage" aria-label="FINSTRIDE on phone and computer">
        <img class="stmt" src="/img/stmt.webp" alt="FINSTRIDE income statement" width="1400" height="698" loading="lazy">
        <img class="scan" src="/img/scan.webp" alt="FINSTRIDE receipt scan" width="600" height="918" loading="lazy">
        <div class="phone"><img src="/img/phone.webp" alt="FINSTRIDE home screen on a phone" width="420" height="1093" loading="lazy"></div>
      </div>
      <div class="in">
        <span class="tagl" style="color:var(--fin)">Open beta · 16 Nov 2026</span>
        <h3>FINSTRIDE</h3>
        <p>Personal finance with the whole picture: budgets, goals, recurring payments, cash-flow forecasts and three financial statements. On the web and as an installable phone app.</p>
        <div class="row"><a class="btn light solid" href="https://apexpaths.co/finstride" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visit FINSTRIDE</a><a class="btn light" href="https://apexpaths.co" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visit ApexPaths</a></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="side">
      <div class="next"><span class="tagl" style="color:var(--av)">In development</span><h3>ACTUVISTA</h3><p>Claims reserving, reported your way. Works from summary data, so no policy-level detail is uploaded.</p><div class="bar"><i style="--w:50%;background:var(--av)"></i></div><div class="bar-l"><span>Base camp</span><span>~50%</span></div></div>
      <div class="next"><span class="tagl" style="color:var(--dp)">Planned</span><h3>DATAPULSE</h3><p>Drop in your spreadsheets, get a dashboard in minutes. Every calculation runs in your browser.</p><div class="bar"><i style="--w:3%;background:var(--dp)"></i></div><div class="bar-l"><span>Base camp</span><span>Next climb</span></div></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section class="sec" id="about"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="sec-head"><h2>Off the CV</h2><p>What a job history leaves out: how I learn, how I work, and what keeps me going.</p></div>
  <div class="trail" id="trail">
    <svg id="switch" aria-hidden="true"><path class="base" id="swBase"/><path class="ink" id="swInk"/></svg>
    <div class="note l"><span class="dot"></span><span class="lab">How I learn</span><h3>Most of my tools were never taught to me.</h3><p>VBA, Qlik, Alteryx, Power BI and Python each arrived because the work needed them, and I learned them on the job. The certificates came later, to fill the gaps. The latest additions are databases, web security and payments.</p></div>
    <div class="note r"><span class="dot"></span><span class="lab">How I work</span><h3>The polishing happens in my own time.</h3><p>Deadlines are kept. If a report could be cleaner, a check tighter or a process faster, I fix it after hours rather than hold the work back. People get the finished version, on time.</p></div>
    <div class="note l"><span class="dot"></span><span class="lab">How I think</span><h3>Every figure should trace back to its source.</h3><p>That's the actuary in me. Give me a system and I want to know how it fits together: where the data comes from, where it breaks, and how to make it easier for the people who rely on it.</p></div>
    <div class="note r"><span class="dot"></span><span class="lab">How I move</span><h3>2026 started with a leap.</h3><p>I left a steady role to grow: a job search in the UAE, a move from Karachi to Lahore, and freelance work. The evenings went into learning how AI is changing data work. One of those evening projects is now an app in open beta.</p></div>
    <div class="note l"><span class="dot"></span><span class="lab">Who keeps me honest</span><h3>My toughest reviewer is at home.</h3><p>Bismah Khalid's notebook started FINSTRIDE, and her feedback shapes every screen. She tests everything before anyone else sees it.</p></div>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section class="sec" id="logbook" style="padding-top:70px"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="sec-head"><h2>Logbook</h2><p>Six camps, in order. Each one lists what was learned there and what came out of it.</p></div>
  <div class="route-wrap" data-now>
    <svg class="rail" aria-hidden="true"><line class="base" x1="30" x2="30" y1="0" y2="100%"/><line class="ink rail-ink" x1="30" x2="30" y1="0" y2="0"/></svg>

    <article class="camp">
      <span class="pin"></span>
      <div class="when"><span class="lab">2009 – 2015</span><small>Bahria University, 2009–2013<br>SZABIST, 2013–2015</small></div>
      <div class="what">
        <h3>Business school</h3>
        <div class="role">BBA Finance · MBA, Business Management and Marketing</div>
        <p class="d">Six years of finance and management, and the first spreadsheet habits.</p>
        <div class="packed"><span class="lab">Packed</span><span class="chip new">Excel</span><span class="count">Kit <b>1</b></span></div>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="camp">
      <span class="pin"></span>
      <div class="when"><span class="lab">2016 – 2017</span><small>SHMA Consulting<br>Karachi · UAE clients</small></div>
      <div class="what">
        <h3>Actuarial Analyst</h3>
        <div class="role">Reporting, reserving, pricing and capital adequacy for insurers</div>
        <p class="d">Turned a manual reporting cycle into Excel macros, and built pricing and reserving models to client requirements.</p>
        <div class="facts"><div class="fact"><b data-n="50" data-pre="~" data-suf="%">~50%</b><span>less time on routine reporting</span></div></div>
        <div class="packed"><span class="lab">Packed</span><span class="chip">Excel</span><span class="chip new">VBA</span><span class="chip new">Reserving</span><span class="chip new">Pricing models</span><span class="count">Kit <b>4</b></span></div>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="camp">
      <span class="pin"></span>
      <div class="when"><span class="lab">2017 – 2021</span><small>SHMA Consulting</small></div>
      <div class="what">
        <h3>Senior Actuarial Analyst</h3>
        <div class="role">Portfolio reviews for ADNIC · reinsurance programme reviews</div>
        <p class="d">Worked in the team building early IFRS 17 base models while the standard was still new, and automated valuation steps with VBA and Qlik.</p>
        <div class="packed"><span class="lab">Packed</span><span class="chip new">Power Query</span><span class="chip new">QlikView</span><span class="chip new">IFRS 17</span><span class="count">Kit <b>7</b></span></div>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="camp">
      <span class="pin"></span>
      <div class="when"><span class="lab">2021 – 2022</span><small>SHMA Consulting</small></div>
      <div class="what">
        <h3>Assistant Manager</h3>
        <div class="role">Actuarial and risk analytics for UAE insurers, including ADNIC</div>
        <p class="d">Led a preliminary Workers' Compensation study for the UAE market, and brought actuarial, claims and reinsurance data together in Alteryx. In the same year:</p>
        <div class="certs">
          <div class="cert">IBM Data Science Professional<small>IBM · Sep 2021</small></div>
          <div class="cert">IBM Data Analyst Professional<small>IBM · Apr 2021</small></div>
          <div class="cert">Applied Data Science with Python<small>University of Michigan · 2021</small></div>
          <div class="cert">Alteryx Designer<small>Alteryx · 2021</small></div>
        </div>
        <a class="credly" href="https://www.credly.com/users/muhammad-babar90" target="_blank" rel="noopener">View all 23 badges on Credly →</a>
        <div class="packed"><span class="lab">Packed</span><span class="chip new">Alteryx</span><span class="chip new">Python</span><span class="chip new">SQL</span><span class="chip new">Qlik Sense</span><span class="count">Kit <b>11</b></span></div>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="camp">
      <span class="pin"></span>
      <div class="when"><span class="lab">2022 – 2026</span><small>Engro Corporation<br>Karachi</small></div>
      <div class="what">
        <h3>Deputy Manager, People Analytics</h3>
        <div class="role">One of Pakistan's largest groups · dashboards for the CPO, CFO and heads of department</div>
        <p class="d">Matched employees across several SAP HCM systems with no shared ID, then moved HR reporting from hand-built Excel to refreshable Power BI and Qlik Sense.</p>
        <div class="facts">
          <div class="fact"><b data-n="1" data-suf="M+">1M+</b><span>workforce data points in one Employee 360 view</span></div>
          <div class="fact"><b data-n="70" data-pre="~" data-suf="%">~70%</b><span>less manual effort behind HR reporting</span></div>
          <div class="fact"><b data-n="2500" data-suf="+">2,500+</b><span>personalised certificates and emails, in Python</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="certs"><div class="cert">Google Data Analytics<small>Google · 2022</small></div></div>
        <div class="packed"><span class="lab">Packed</span><span class="chip new">Power BI</span><span class="chip new">SAP SuccessFactors</span><span class="count">Kit <b>13</b></span></div>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="camp">
      <span class="pin"></span>
      <div class="when"><span class="lab">2026 – now</span><small>Lahore</small></div>
      <div class="what">
        <h3>Freelance, and ApexPaths</h3>
        <div class="role">Data &amp; BI consultant · Founder of ApexPaths · Co-founder of FINSTRIDE</div>
        <p class="d">Client work in Excel, Power Query and Power BI by day. In the evenings, a household budget model became FINSTRIDE: a web and mobile app with two-step login, offline entry and payments in testing.</p>
        <div class="packed"><span class="lab">Packed</span><span class="chip new">Flask</span><span class="chip new">PostgreSQL</span><span class="chip new">JavaScript</span><span class="chip new">Web security</span><span class="chip new">Payments</span><span class="count">Kit <b>18</b></span></div>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
</div></section>
</Base>
